[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Moving a node between files

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-ON-DISK-MOVES
TITLE: Moving a node between files
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: rows
STATEMENT: >>>
Retention class changes by file move; what survives collection; where a backlog item lives.

- A node changes retention class only by moving its file; the UID never changes. Thirteen relocations have held. A dangling relation is fatal; a dangling fingerprint is silent; both are scanned. [WORKS]
- The grid says what survives when a plan is collected — its claims — but not where a surviving claim goes. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-MEMBERSHIP-AND-COLLECTION-CONTRADICT]. [UNADDRESSED]
- Two nodes still say handover freezes the whole plan. A later mechanism narrowed that to the scope handed over. See [LINK: DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN], [LINK: MECH-PLAN-BEADS-SNAPSHOT] and [LINK: MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION] and [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-MECHANISM]. [FALLS OUT: MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS]
- Is a backlog item canon (reviewed) or beads (private)? An unreviewed sketch node sitting on the branch is neither. Feeds [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-MEMBERSHIP-AND-COLLECTION-CONTRADICT]. [GAP]
- The beads-migration plan's authoritative source is a rendered artifact plus private markdown, neither in the repo. Which one wins is undecided. See [LINK: DEC-SOURCE-OUT-OF-REPO]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]. [OPEN: DEC-SOURCE-OUT-OF-REPO]
- The reason given for putting architecture beside code — 'plans decay and are collected' — is the lean that was since dropped. The placement itself still stands. See [LINK: DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION]. Speaks about [LINK: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-DECISION]. [OPEN: DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION]
- Scribe's move renames a file outside its load-change-save pipeline, so no joint fires. The library form has no move at all. [GAP]
<<<
